          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most travel trailers and motorhomes, the Dometic Brisk II 13,500 BTU is the best camper air conditioner: correctly sized, easy to service and easy to power, especially with a soft starter. Long rigs and hot climates call for the Coleman Mach 15, and the Furrion Chill 14.5K is the natural replacement on trailers that shipped with it. Small campers are better served by a 5,000 BTU window unit on shore power or a WAVE 3 or Zero Breeze Mark 3 off grid.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before you buy anything, check your power. A 30 amp pedestal, a 2,200 watt generator or a 2kWh battery each set a ceiling on what you can run, and the best AC in the world is useless if it trips the breaker. Add a soft starter, keep the filters and coils clean, and size for the climate you actually camp in.
